                    coach_intro:            `Three clocks are running: the retailer wants a signed letter of intent in 45 days, the Córdoba rival is bidding for the same listing, and Don Aldo has heart surgery in June. This is not only a finance problem — it is a transition in how Aldo leads, from doing-and-controlling to building-and-delegating. Capability, not capital, is the first thing that breaks; the 75-day terms turn profit into a cash question; and family relationships are a strategic asset, not a private matter. Make the four decisions tell one coherent transition.`,

